{"kind":"request","text":"RB-1: bound one rule row and the attribution history of an item.\n\nFound by builder audit 7f6f6834 on ruling 9753818f. The facts at\nmain a200cd0a:\n- A `rule` row holds the whole subjects of the rule input\n  (`derive/src/guards.ts:133-137`). No check bounds its bytes in a\n  scope without the capacity opt-in.\n- A subject holds `Item.attributed`, the history of each author and\n  principal. `withMembers` (`derive/src/attribution.ts:16-19`) appends\n  each new reference with no count check. `partyMembers` bounds the\n  present party list and not this history.\nSo no constant bounds one rule row, and no constant bounds one item.\n\nScene: a scope runs for years with many authors. Each item and each\nrule input stays under a stated byte ceiling, and the validator of\nthe definition proves the ceiling.\n\nThis is design work first, and it is kernel work: a ceiling changes\nthe inputs that a scope accepts, so replay must agree. Before the\ncode, write a short design note and send it for my ruling:\n1. Each reader of `attributed`, and which readers need the whole\n   history.\n2. The candidate bounds for `attributed`, with what each one loses.\n3. A ceiling for one rule row in every scope, its refusal, and what\n   replay checks.\n4. What a scope that is already past a ceiling does.\n\nOrder: after the client chain and H1. RB-1 does not hold the cutover\ndeployment. The total of the CDF-1 head stops each new act at\n`scopeBytes`.","body":{"conditions":"Planner rules on the design note before code; kernel review that cites docs/kernel.md section 7; each item and each rule input has a stated byte ceiling in every scope; replay checks the same ceiling; gate passes; checker reviews with the Security conclusion","stale_bases":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:7f6f683440b8f4c79742cc638cc287cc2a026b82 stale; retired bases: git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:b5750e6e82650d29470d64f83b0dc3a50115b466","target_head":"a200cd0a5999852eb9142136d2b11e2b7c87e02b","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_repo":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}